   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);border:none;line-height:1.2\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">This week at D-RUG we&#39;ll have a talk from Robert Hijmans.  Robert is the author of the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">raster</code> package - the essential way to deal with gridded spatial data in R, as well as the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">dismo</code> (species distribution modeling) and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">geosphere</code> (spherical trigonometry) packages.  He also teaches GEO200CN - Quantitative geography, not to mention his <a href=\"http://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=NWdPabcAAAAJ&amp;view_op=list_works&amp;pagesize=100\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://scholar.google.com/citations?hl%3Den%26user%3DNWdPabcAAAAJ%26view_op%3Dlist_works%26pagesize%3D100&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792469594369000&amp;usg=AOvVaw04PPxztJINtZZe4ICk1Fwj\">great research on species distribution modeling</a> .Robert will give a talk about tools for spatial analysis in R.  Come with your spatial/geographic analysis questions!</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Note that this week&#39;s D-RUG will be in <strong>2120J Wickson</strong> - this is the room just to the right of our regular meeting space.  It will at the usual time: <strong>1-3 PM</strong>, with the usual snacks.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">See you there!</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam</p>\r\n</div><div><div></div><div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
